  <div class="content-column">

    <section id="about">
      <div class="section-header"><h2>About Me</h2></div>
      <div class="formal-font">
        <p>I am a <strong>Ph.D. student</strong> at the <a href="https://disl-lab.github.io" class="lnk">Data Intelligence System Lab (DISL)</a> at KAIST, where I am advised by <strong>Prof. Hwanjun Song</strong>. I first joined the lab for my M.S. and then continued into the integrated Ph.D. program, after studying Economics with a double major in Statistics at Yonsei University.</p>
        <p>My work centers on <strong>Retrieval-Augmented Generation</strong>, where I build frameworks that keep generation faithful to retrieved evidence and design evaluation methods that reveal when they fail. The same interest carries into <strong>human-AI alignment</strong> and <strong>LLM agent simulation</strong>, and more recently into <strong>Physical AI</strong>, where I am exploring world model-based robot learning and sim-to-real transfer.</p>
        <div class="highlight-box">
          <p><strong><i class="fas fa-lightbulb" style="color:var(--accent);margin-right:.4rem"></i>Open to collaboration.</strong>
          I'm always happy to discuss RAG, LLM evaluation, and agent simulation. Feel free to reach out by email.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
    <section id="research">
      <div class="section-header"><h2>Research Overview</h2></div>
      <div class="formal-font">
        <blockquote>"My work follows one thread, from grounding what a model says in evidence, to measuring whether that grounding holds, to agents that act on it in simulated and physical worlds."</blockquote>
        <div class="thrust-grid">
          <div class="thrust-card">
            <h3><i class="fas fa-magnifying-glass" style="color:var(--accent)"></i> Robust RAG Frameworks</h3>
            <p>Retrieval and generation that stays faithful to source evidence, through query expansion and extraction-generation alignment.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="thrust-card">
            <h3><i class="fas fa-scale-balanced" style="color:var(--accent)"></i> Evaluation &amp; Reliability</h3>
            <p>Benchmarks and automatic evaluators that expose where RAG systems break, from query-agnostic metrics to multi-agent relevance annotation.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="thrust-card">
            <h3><i class="fas fa-robot" style="color:var(--accent)"></i> LLM Agent Simulation</h3>
            <p>Language models that simulate multi-party behavior, including seller-buyer retail dynamics and multimodal conflict mediation.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="thrust-card">
            <h3><i class="fas fa-microchip" style="color:var(--accent)"></i> Physical AI</h3>
            <p>World model-based robot learning and sim-to-real transfer, extending agent reasoning to systems that act in the physical world.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
